@namespace SIMF.Components.Forms

@* The read-only record view.

   Six grids across four Control Panel pages offered Edit and Delete as the only
   ways to open a row. Once those buttons were permission-gated, an admin holding
   View but neither mutating code could no longer read a single record at all,
   and the actions column rendered as an empty box. Details is the read
   affordance those grids were missing; it needs no permission of its own,
   because seeing the row is what the page's View code already bought.

   The ~20 *ViewDelete components hand-write the same dt/dd block and are
   deliberately NOT migrated onto this: they already render inside CrudShell's
   dialog frame, so wrapping them here would nest a SimfModal inside a modal,
   which SimfModal forbids outright ("NOT STACKABLE"). They are a separate
   mechanism for the same job, not debt this was meant to pay off.

   Rendered behind @if (Open) rather than toggling SimfModal's own Open, to match
   SimfConfirm exactly. Details opens and closes far more often than a one-shot
   dialog, and the two forms leave SimfModal through different JS unbind paths;
   matching the sibling keeps this on the path every CP page already exercises. *@

@if (Open)
{
    <SimfModal Open="true"
               Title="@Title"
               OnClose="OnClose"
               CloseLabel="@CloseLabel">
        <ChildContent>
            <dl class="simf-dl">
                @ChildContent
            </dl>
        </ChildContent>
    </SimfModal>
}

@code {
    /// <summary>Whether the details view is showing.</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool Open { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Modal heading - normally the record's own name.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string Title { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    /// <summary>Label for the close control.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string CloseLabel { get; set; } = "Close";

    /// <summary>Raised when the reader dismisses the view.</summary>
    [Parameter] public EventCallback OnClose { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The <see cref="SimfDetailRow"/> entries to show.</summary>
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? ChildContent { get; set; }
}
